# MCSP Driver Builder Interface 0.52

Status: Constructive interface experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parents:
- ASSEMBLER-SEED-0.40.mcsp
- DISASSEMBLER-SEED-0.41.mcsp
- DECOMPILER-SEED-0.42.mcsp
- CLOSED-ROUND-TRIP-0.43.mcsp
- HEX-POSSIBILITY-LAYER-0.44.mcsp
- HARDWARE-BOUNDARY-RECONCILIATION-0.51.mcsp

## Objective

Place MCSP immediately behind the driver-building boundary.

A driver builder may consume an MCSP hardware-boundary report and reuse MCSP
assembly machinery to construct a target-machine realization. MCSP then verifies
the resulting realization through disassembly and decompilation before accepting
REALIZE.

MCSP does not own the resulting driver merely because its construction machinery
was reused.

## Driver-builder report

A bounded machine-representable report contains:

    semantic_relation
    semantic_width
    destination_role
    source_role
    encoding_form
    hardware_target
    applicability
    qualification
    unresolved_residue

The report states obligations and boundary information. It does not prescribe
driver architecture, operating-system policy, lifecycle, ownership, or deployment.

## Construction path

    DETERMINATE CONDITION / semantic obligation
        -> hardware boundary
        -> MCSP driver-builder report
        -> driver builder
        -> MCSP ASSEMBLER
        -> target encoding
        -> MCSP DISASSEMBLER
        -> reconstructed structural tuple
        -> MCSP DECOMPILER
        -> reconstructed semantic obligation
        -> compare with report
        -> REALIZE / SUSPEND / REJECT

## Authority rule

The semantic obligation is authoritative over the realization.

The machine encoding is evidence of realization, not semantic authority.
The driver builder retains implementation choice inside the report constraints.
MCSP qualification accepts only a realization that preserves the report obligation.

## Reuse rule

A driver builder may reuse the MCSP Assembler without adopting MCSP as the driver's
runtime, scheduler, state machine, type system, or operating-system abstraction.

Reuse is therefore construction reuse, not ownership transfer or semantic inversion.

## Bounded 0.52 fixture

Report:

    relation = EXCLUSIVE
    width = 64
    destination = 0
    source = 3
    form = 1
    hardware = x86-64

MCSP Assembler projection:

    48 31 D8

MCSP Disassembler reconstructs the same structural tuple.
MCSP Decompiler reconstructs the exclusive relation and its truth obligation.

Only after report/tuple/semantic agreement may the bounded path return REALIZE.

## Failure containment

Unknown/unsupported target construction -> SUSPEND.
Encoding inconsistent with report -> REJECT.
Disassembled tuple inconsistent with report -> REJECT.
Decompiled semantics inconsistent with report -> REJECT.
Unresolved residue incompatible with qualification -> SUSPEND or REJECT according
to whether compatibility is unresolved or contradicted.

## Boundary

0.52 is a driver-builder interface witness, not a production driver generator.
It does not claim operating-system driver integration, arbitrary ISA assembly,
device discovery, deployment, signing, privileged installation, or universal
hardware support.

Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
STATE and TYPE remain derived and unnecessary to this interface.
